    "interpretation": "These are the original authors' own genomic response predictors, deployed by them on their own patients. Both were developed on this cohort (Hatzis et al. 2011), so they are IN-SAMPLE and their effect sizes are inflated; they cannot be read as prospective added value. What they do establish is that the nested LRT, on these patients with this four-axis base model, detects added value when a genuinely informative transcriptomic predictor is present. The instrument is not inert.",
    "contrast": "ggi_class -- a published prognostic signature the authors computed but did NOT fit to pCR -- is null by their deployment and null by ours. The redundancy result is therefore reproduced by the original authors' own scoring, not an artefact of cohort-free deployment."
